# Probe of slice 307 (the review of Codex, item 4; not a fixture of the suite): a Structure field whose leaf is a number of another
# type at a Structure formal -- CG (CPoint: p; int: q 7) given to g (Point: p; int: q), where CPoint (char: x '1'; int: y 2) has the
# leaf x of another number type than Point's x and the program defines the char -> int receiver.  On a23 the translation admitted the
# field by the Consumer-relative projection with the conversion table and both executors stopped R0 at run time (an uncaught implicit
# throw: the entry reception of the field is kind-strict; the probe p307l).  Since a24 the applicability is kind-strict at the leaves
# too, as the ordinary admission and the kernel are, and this program is refused at translation ("implements is false in function
# argument"); the conversion table at nested leaves is a remainder shared by the translation and the executors.  Entry 7; 80: the check.
Point:
    int: x 1
    int: y 2
end: Point
CPoint:
    char: x '1'
    int: y 2
end: CPoint
CG:
    CPoint: p
    int: q 7
end: CG
Calls:
    int: n 0
end: Calls
fn: lm_stg_convert_char_int (char: v) int
    Calls\n: Calls\n + 1
    return: (cast: (int) v)
end: lm_stg_convert_char_int
fn: g (Point: p; int: q) int
    return: p\x + p\y + q
end: g
fn: by_fields () int
    return: g(CG)
end: by_fields
fn: run () int
    if: by_fields() != 58
        return: 80
    return: 7
end: run
int: code run()
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
